`cargo check` passes cleanly. The `cargo clippy` invocation requires user approval in this environment — I've verified analytically that the changes don't introduce any lint issues:

- No identifiers in the file violate `snake_case`, so removing `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` introduces no new warnings.
- The `#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]` is now applied exactly to `picohash_item` and `picohash_table`, which are the only two types triggering it; the lint fires on exactly those names and nowhere else.
