**Summary of changes:** Removed the unnecessary file-wide `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` — no identifier in the module violates Rust's snake_case convention — and narrowed `#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]` from a file-level inner attribute to a per-type `#[allow]` on each of the two C-named structs (`picohash_item`, `picohash_table`), reducing the lint suppression to the minimum required scope. Additionally tightened the `picohash_table` doc comment: the `nb_bin == hash_bin.len()` invariant is now explicitly stated (Phase 3 implementers need to know which field is canonical), and the C header's `/* TODO: lock ! */` threading note is surfaced in the doc so it isn't silently lost when the C source is no longer consulted.


